[00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.300]   Good morning, and welcome to Earthstone Energy's second quarter 2020 conference call.
[00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.120]   At this time, I'll present you in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.460]   A brief question and answer session will follow the formal presentation.
[00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.340]   If anyone should require your assistance during the conference, please press star zero on your telephone keypad.
[00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.040]   As a reminder, this conference is being recorded.
[00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.780]   Joining us today from Earthstone are Robert Anderson, President and Chief Executive Officer,
[00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.720]   Mark Lumpkin, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer,
[00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.560]   and Scott Fielander, Vice President of Finance.
[00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.180]   Mr. Fielander, you may begin.
[00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.120]   Thank you, and welcome to our second quarter conference call.
[00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.920]   Before we get started, I would like to remind you that today's call will contain forward-looking statements
[00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.920]   within the meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933 as amended,
[00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.660]   and Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 as amended.
[00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.880]   Although management believes these statements are based on reasonable expectations,
[00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.580]   they can give no assurance that they will prove to be correct.
[00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.400]   These statements are subject to certain risks, uncertainties, and assumptions,
[00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.260]   as described in the earnings announcement we released yesterday,
[00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:22.140]   and in our 2019 annual report on Form 10-K and subsequent quarterly filings.
[00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.800]   These documents can be found in the Investors section of our website,
[00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.540]   www.ncb.gov, or www.ncb.gov.
[00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.560]   www.ncb.gov.com.
[00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.560]   Should one or more of these risks materialize, or should underlying assumptions prove incorrect,
[00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.560]   actual results may vary materially.
[00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:45.560]   This conference call also includes references to certain non-GAPS financial measures,
[00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:52.560]   which include adjusted diluted shares, adjusted EBITDAX, adjusted net income, all-in cash costs,
[00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.560]   cash G&A, and free cash flow.
[00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.560]   Reconciliation of these statements are not in the form of a direct, or a direct, or a direct,
[00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.560]   cash flow.
[00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.560]   These non-GAPS financial measures, to the most directly comparable measure under GAPS,
[00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.560]   are contained in our earnings announcement released yesterday.
[00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:14.560]   Also, please note, information on this call speaks only as of today, August 6, 2020.
